abstract: >-
  End-to-end computational pipeline for Bayesian identification of
  interspecies interaction parameters in a 5-species oral biofilm
  Hamilton ODE model using Transitional Markov Chain Monte Carlo
  (TMCMC), and propagation of posterior uncertainty through Dysbiotic
  Index (DI) mapping to 3D finite element stress analysis (Abaqus).
  Includes multiscale coupling (0D ODE → 1D/2D reaction-diffusion
  PDE → 3D FEM) with spatially non-uniform growth eigenstrain derived
  from Monod-type nutrient consumption. Species modelled: Streptococcus
  oralis, Actinomyces naeslundii, Veillonella dispar, Fusobacterium
  nucleatum, Porphyromonas gingivalis.

